// The open-decides push path: `ys` is a bare `List.empty()`, so `push` is what
// would decide its element, and the argument `xs` is itself open. The slot
// would then hold the marker (`List<List<Unit>>`), so `push` refuses the
// element: decide `xs` first, or write its type on the binding.
fun main() {
    var ys = List.empty()
    var xs = List.empty()
    ys.push(xs)
    print(ys.len())
}
